\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3.2 Game Modes\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 FlexWord Classic:
\f1\b0  The curated "One-a-day" puzzle. Everyone plays the same word.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Infinite Mode:
\f1\b0  Unlimited procedural puzzles for practice.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Campaign / Ladder:
\f1\b0  The "Hero's Journey." Start with 3-letter words (Educational engine) and graduate to 4, 5, and eventually 8-letter "Boss Battles."\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Daily Standard Race Pack (DSRP):
\f1\b0  A competitive daily set of varying lengths (e.g., one 3-letter, one 4-letter, two 5-letter words).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3.3 Difficulty Logic\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Standard:
\f1\b0  6 Guesses. Solution is a "Common" word. Guesses can be any "Valid" word.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Hard:
\f1\b0  6 Guesses. No hints. Must use revealed clues (Strict Mode).\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Very Hard:
\f1\b0  Every guess must be a potential solution to the puzzle based on current information.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Extreme (The "Insane" Tier):
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The "Safety Net" is removed.\
\ls4\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The 
\f0\b Solution Pool
\f1\b0  is expanded to equal the 
\f0\b Total Valid Guess Pool
\f1\b0  (approx. 15k words for 5-letter puzzles).\
\ls4\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Guesses that are not in the dictionary result in a "Lost Turn" (Meep Meep error) rather than just a "Try Again" shake.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

